# Owner decision 2026-11-15, an unrun command draft ("@question …", "@improve …"): ⌘⏎ runs it as ⏎ does; the focus
# leaving discards it; any other ⌘ shortcut discards it and goes on to the app.
# QUESTION: the format has no "the command ran" check. Nothing of the draft reaching the field and the panel staying up
# (with the request or its answer) is the closest; the Mac adapter or a later EXPECT could check the request itself.
NAME cmd+Return runs an unrun command draft as Return does, nothing of it reaching the field
PROFILES all
LANG english
TEXT "Hi |"
TYPE "@question hi"
EXPECT marked "question › hi"   # a command draft shows as its name › its text
EXPECT panel shown
KEY cmd+enter
EXPECT doc "Hi |"
EXPECT panel shown
